    "title": "Jeremy Peña homers in rehab start for Sugar Land with potential return to Astros as soon as Friday - NewsBreak",
    "text": "Shortstop Jeremy Peña homered in his second and potentially final rehab game with Triple-A Sugar Land before rejoining the Houston Astros from a fractured rib. Peña went 1-for-4 with a home run, a lineout, a groundout and a flyout in Sugar Land’s game Wednesday against Tacoma. He played seven innings at shortstop after serving as designated hitter in his first rehab game Tuesday. Astros manager Joe Espada said the team would “see how (Peña) feels” after playing Wednesday and “there’s a possibility” of his returning during their series in Boston that begins Friday. Peña has been sidelined since June 27, when he sustained the rib fracture on a hit-by-pitch. He ranked second among major-league players in wins above replacement, per Baseball Reference, at the time of his injury. Cristian Javier, making his fourth rehab start in his recovery from Tommy John surgery, threw 3⅓ innings for Sugar Land on Wednesday. Javier allowed two hits, walked four batters and struck out three. Espada said Wednesday morning Javier was targeted to build up to 50-to-60 pitches. Javier threw 64 pitches in the outing, 33 for strikes. Sign up for Houston Chronicle newsletters here Read the original article on houstonchronicle.com",
